<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20397" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Helvĭi</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Helvi</span></b> ), ōrum,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				people of</i> Gallia Narbonensis, <i>whose
			capital</i>, <i>called</i> Alba Helvorum <i>and</i> Alba Helvia, <i>was celebrated
				for its wine</i>, now <i>Alps</i>, in <i>Viviers</i>, <i>Départ.
				Ardèche</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 7, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">75</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">id. B.
				C. 1, 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 4, 5, § 36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14, 3, 4, §
			43</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Helvĭcus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to the Helvii</i>, <i>Helvian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 1, 3, § 18</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
